                <invention-title lang="de">VIDEOCODIERUNGSVERFAHREN, VIDEODECODIERUNGSVERFAHREN UND VORRICHTUNG DAMIT</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">PROCÉDÉ DE CODAGE VIDÉO, PROCÉDÉ DE DÉCODAGE VIDÉO, ET DISPOSITIF S'Y RAPPORTANT</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">VIDEO ENCODING METHOD, VIDEO DECODING METHOD, AND DEVICE USING SAME</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The present invention relates to a video decoding method, a video encoding method, and a decoder-readable storage medium storing the encoded video information generated by the video encoding method. The video encoding method comprises the steps of (S2410) partitioning a current picture into one or more tiles and one or more slices and (52420) encoding the current picture based on the one or more tiles and the one or more slices to (S2430) generate encoded video information. The encoded video information includes information on a tile which is a rectangular region comprising largest coding units and information on a slice comprising a sequence of consecutive largest coding units. In the current picture, the slice is configured to contain an integer number of complete tiles when the slice includes tiles, and the tile is configured to contain an integer number of complete slices when the tile includes slices. When the slice is configured to contain the integer number of compete tiles, all coding tree units in each of the integer number of compete tiles belong to the slice, and when the tile is configured to contain the integer number of complete slices, all coding tree units in each of the integer number of compete slices belong to the tile.</p>
            </abstract>
